    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39939" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā^drŭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		quattuor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>fourcornered</i> or <i>fourfold</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">errabam riguis per quadrua compita in hortis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>laid out in squares</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 14, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vis,</span>”
				<i>fourfold</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 842</span></i>
			.</div>
